After executing VACUUM labs.person, the physical page still contained the existing tuples, but dead tuples generated by previous UPDATE and DELETE operations were marked as reusable. The command cleaned transaction visibility information and allowed PostgreSQL to reuse free space in future insert operations. However, the physical structure of the table and tuple locations (ctid) remained unchanged.
After executing VACUUM FULL labs.person, PostgreSQL rewrote the entire table into a new compact physical structure. All dead tuples were physically removed, free space was reclaimed, and the table size was reduced. As a result, tuple locations (ctid) could change because the rows were copied into newly organized pages.
